    <h1>A 27B 1-bit LLM<br>on one RISC-V core</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      When every weight is a single bit, the multiply disappears and a matmul becomes a pure
      data-layout problem. The stock llama.cpp kernel answers it with <b>a quarter of the vector
      lanes and one output row at a time</b>. Fixing the layout, then handing the reduction to a
      stock Andes vendor instruction, made decode <b>11.86x faster</b> on a 27B model - with
      bit-identical results.
    </p>

